	Tooltip: ""
}

CyberwareOfflineChip: {
	DisplayName: Chip de desconexión de ciberimplantes
	Tooltip: ""
}

Mewtwo: {
	DisplayName: Chip Supersueño
	Tooltip: "Úsalo para entrar al Supersueño"
}

RapidBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón rápido
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El fuego sostenido aumenta la temperatura del cañón: cuanto más caliente está, más rápido dispara, lanzando rayos al rojo vivo hasta alcanzar una incandescencia blanca que desprende cenizas fundidas
		Al llegar al límite del indicador, se activa una válvula de sobrecalentamiento durante varios segundos: aplica una cadencia de fuego máxima sin coste de maná, con vapor saliendo a borbotones por la boca del cañón bajo el sonido de una alarma estridente
		A continuación se produce un enfriamiento forzado con una cadencia de disparo muy reducida; el calor se disipa lentamente mientras se mantiene el fuego: controla el calor, mantente en el límite.
		'''
}

FocusBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon de enfoque
	Tooltip: Obliga a los tres haces de seguimiento a converger en un único y devastador impacto concentrado
}

PrecisionOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor de precisión
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Juicio calibrado: elimina toda la dispersión; los impactos consecutivos sin fallos aumentan la calibración
		Al alcanzar 15 acumulaciones, dispara un rayo de juicio perforante con crítico garantizado; si falla un rayo, se reinicia la calibración
		'''
}

OverloadCoreModule: {
	DisplayName: Núcleo de sobrecarga
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Desactiva el bloqueo de seguridad del orbe: sigue cargándolo más allá del máximo para sobrecargarlo — hasta duplicar el daño y ampliar el radio de la explosión
		Si mantienes la carga más allá de la línea roja, el núcleo se romperá en tus manos, te lanzará hacia atrás y quemará la mitad de tu maná
		'''
}

SteadyStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata estable
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Las pausas entre disparos cargan un condensador de voltaje, que se muestra en un indicador situado sobre tu cabeza; al disparar, este se descarga para potenciar toda la ráfaga
		Una descarga completa añade perforación y filigrana de voltaje, pero la carga completa solo se mantiene durante un breve lapso antes de descarizarse por completo: los disparos deliberados y mesurados son los mejores, mientras que mantener apretado el gatillo apenas carga nada
		En modo láser, al activar el rayo se descarga la carga almacenada, lo que provoca una breve oleada de daño de eco
		'''
}

HarmonyGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre armonioso
	Tooltip:
		'''
		La bioconducción reduce el coste de maná; el maná derramado al golpear se condensa en volutas resonantes que se esparcen por el campo de batalla
		Las volutas vuelven hacia ti: al recoger una, se restaura maná y se acumulan "Armonías" que aumentan la velocidad de ataque (hasta 5)
		'''
}

ResonanceFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco de resonancia
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Metrónomo de onda estacionaria: cuenta tus disparos; cada cuarto disparo se convierte en un rayo rítmico resonante —más denso, más potente y capaz de atravesar un objetivo adicional—.
		Al impactar, el rayo rítmico genera una onda oscilatoria en forma de anillo que inflige daño de área y empuja suavemente a los enemigos hacia fuera.
		Mantener el ritmo acumula tempo para potenciar los siguientes golpes; si se hace una pausa demasiado larga, el tempo se reinicia
		En modo láser, la columna pulsa a un ritmo fijo; los golpes que impactan dentro de la ventana rítmica también desatan la onda
		'''
}

AdaptiveOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor adaptativo
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Control predictivo de disparo: analiza el movimiento del objetivo y proyecta un marcador holográfico de anticipación en el punto de interceptación
		Los rayos se desvían automáticamente para anticiparse a los disparos; los impactos contra objetivos en movimiento activan ataques adaptativos adicionales
		'''
}

AssaultStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata de asalto
	Tooltip:
		'''
		La culata incorpora dos cápsulas de combate gemelas: al empuñar el arma, se despliegan un par de brazos armados flotantes a la altura de los hombros
		Los brazos se sincronizan con el gatillo, alternando disparos de apoyo rápidos con cada tiro que realizas
		'''
}

BalancedGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre equilibrado
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Protocolo de Equilibrio Dual: los impactos de rayo generan carga Yang, mientras que los orbes de carga generan carga Yin
		Mientras ambas cargas se mantengan en equilibrio, la balanza se alinea: el daño, la cadencia de disparo y la eficiencia de maná aumentan
		'''
}

CapacitorBankModule: {
	DisplayName: Banco de condensadores
	Tooltip:
		'''
		La carga ilumina una rejilla de seis celdas de condensador situada en lo alto, una a una, a medida que se va llenando el orbe
		Una vez que el orbe sale disparado, la rejilla se queda atrás y se descarga celda a celda, lanzando arcos de alimentación hacia el orbe en vuelo
		Cada arco que impacta aporta daño adicional y aumenta el radio de explosión del orbe: cuanto más lejos vuela, más fuerte es el impacto
		'''
}

CrystalGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre de cristal
	Tooltip: El cristal dieléctrico sintético entra en resonancia con el usuario, reduciendo el coste de maná y aumentando la probabilidad de crítico, pero ralentizando la recarga
}

EfficientGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre eficaz
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Protocolo Bucle sin pérdidas: los impactos de los rayos y el láser recuperan energía del coste de maná de cada disparo, condensando las células de reciclaje que orbitan a tu alrededor.
		Cuando alcances las ocho células, tu próximo clic izquierdo se convertirá en un "Tiro sin pérdidas": se te reembolsará todo el maná y cada célula inundará la boca del cañón para potenciar esa ráfaga
		En modo láser, el "Tiro sin pérdidas" descarga todas las células en tu cursor, detonando la energía recuperada
		'''
}

HeavyBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón pesado
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El estriado reforzado aplasta la dispersión y la cadencia; cada disparo impacta como una profunda hendidura
		Los impactos del rayo y del láser en el mismo objetivo tallan muescas; la cuarta muesca asesta un mazazo demoledor
		El mazazo inflige un golpe crítico garantizado, cuya intensidad se calcula en función de tu hendidura más profunda, y rompe temporalmente la armadura del objetivo (la ruptura solo beneficia a tus propios impactos)
		'''
}

HighVoltageCoreModule: {
	DisplayName: Núcleo de alta tensión
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un condensador de alta tensión se carga con cada golpe
		Cuando está completamente cargado, tu siguiente golpe descarga un arco penetrante que sale de tu cuerpo y atraviesa todo lo que se encuentra a su paso
		'''
}

HoloOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor holográfico
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Proyector de rejilla táctica: despliega periódicamente una rejilla holográfica alrededor del cursor mientras luchas
		Los proyectiles hostiles que la tocan se desintegran; los rayos que la atraviesan se recalibran, se potencian y se reorientan
		'''
}

HypersonicBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón hipersónico
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El estriado del motor estatoreactor hace que los rayos se aceleren en vuelo; al romper la barrera del sonido se desencadena una onda de choque en forma de anillo de sujeción
		Una vez superada la barrera, los rayos se vuelven incandescentes: aplica daño adicional, mayor penetración y una estela de condensación de vapor
		'''
}

KineticDamperModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata con amortiguador cinético
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los amortiguadores hidráulicos almacenan el retroceso de tus golpes como reserva cinética; por encima de la mitad de la reserva, no puedes ser empujado hacia atrás
		En el momento en que recibes daño, toda la reserva se libera en forma de una onda sísmica contraria que lanza a los enemigos por los aires
		'''
}

LightStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata ligera
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El armazón ligero segmentado aumenta la cadencia de disparo y convierte cada rayo principal en una cadena de luz que se arrastra:
		dos segmentos de la cadena se deslizan a lo largo de la trayectoria del rayo, cada uno de los cuales inflige su propio daño
		'''
}

MultiCellFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco multicelular
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Protocolo de alimentación de la matriz: despliega una matriz energética de seis celdas a tu alrededor; cada ráfaga que impacta carga una celda, mientras que el láser de prisma se carga más lentamente
		Una vez que las seis celdas están iluminadas, la matriz se activa y dispara una salva de seis rayos autoguiados contra el objetivo desde las posiciones de las celdas; a continuación, se vacía y se bloquea brevemente para enfriarse
		'''
}

PlasmaInjectorModule: {
	DisplayName: Inyector de plasma
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Inyecta plasma de alta entalpía en la esfera: su detonación deja tras de sí un sol de plasma en miniatura
		El sol abrasa todo lo que hay a su alrededor y azota periódicamente al enemigo más cercano con erupciones solares
		'''
}

QuantumFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco cuántico
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Protocolo de entrelazamiento: al golpear dos objetivos diferentes de forma consecutiva, estos quedan entrelazados cuánticamente durante unos segundos
		El daño infligido a cualquiera de ellos se transmite parcialmente al otro; cuando uno muere, el vínculo se rompe y el eco acumulado se descarga sobre el superviviente
		'''
}

ScattershotBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón de dispersión
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El cañón fracturado divide cada disparo en una ráfaga de rayos de corto alcance; 
		al impactar por primera vez o al final de su trayectoria, cada rayo se fragmenta en un cono de fragmentos de luz cristalina
		Los fragmentos nunca alcanzan su objetivo y su daño disminuye drásticamente con la distancia: una ráfaga a quemarropa clava todo el grupo en un solo objetivo,
		mientras que los disparos lejanos solo rozan
		La detonación del orbe de carga también provoca una explosión de fragmentos de gran tamaño a lo largo de su trayectoria de vuelo
		'''
}

ThermalOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor térmico
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Proporciona marcas térmicas a los objetivos, calcinando a la presa hasta que pasa de un rojo hierro a la incandescencia en la visión térmica;
		a máxima potencia, se activa el bloqueo al rojo vivo, y los rayos se clavan con fuerza en ese objetivo con un bonus de crítico y un efecto abrasador sostenido
		'''
}

VolatileFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco volátil
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El campo de contención del armazón se desestabiliza: cada rayo nace con una mutación caótica aleatoria,
		marcada por un efecto de interferencia superpuesto en su color de mutación
		Fisión (cian) se bifurca en pleno vuelo; Sobrecarga (rojo) duplica el daño con una trayectoria frenética;
		Inestable (naranja) detona al primer impacto; Aberrante (morado) se desvía hacia el enemigo más cercano
		En modo láser, el campo se intensifica periódicamente: las intensificaciones de Sobrecarga provocan daño adicional,
		mientras que las de Inestable detonan tras acumular varios impactos
		'''
}

NovaBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon Nova
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un cañón de plasma sobrecargado genera un microimpulso en el punto de impacto de cada rayo
		El precio es una dispersión mayor, un impacto por disparo más débil y un mayor consumo de maná
		'''
}

PrismOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor prismático
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un prisma de fase situado al final de la trayectoria óptica divide cada haz en dos ramificaciones al salir
		Los haces primarios recorren una distancia ligeramente menor a cambio de una ventana crítica más nítida
		'''
}

TeslaCoreModule: {
	DisplayName: Núcleo tesla
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los arcos eléctricos de alta tensión hacen que los rayos lanzados alcancen al enemigo más cercano
		Cada nodo encadenado hereda los efectos al impactar, con un coste de maná mayor
		'''
}

RecoilStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata de retroceso
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un amortiguador de sobrecarga convierte las detonaciones de los orbes en propulsión cinética para el portador
		El alcance del rayo se amplía al mismo tiempo; el gatillo se nota un poco lento
		'''
}

SwarmGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre en enjambre
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un agarre de malla neuronal libera un enjambre de microesferas con un potente sistema de guiado en el momento en que la esfera detona
		La velocidad de las esferas disminuye y el consumo de maná aumenta como compensación
		'''
}

GravityFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco gravitatorio
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un anillo de singularidad en miniatura convierte el orbe de energía en un pozo gravitatorio
		Atrae a los enemigos cercanos hacia su núcleo mientras se carga, y el radio de detonación se amplía considerablemente
		La cámara de precisión hace que la carga resulte un poco más pesada
		'''
}

LaserBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón láser prismático
	Tooltip: Convierte el haz fusionado en una columna láser prismática continua, a costa de un enorme consumo de maná y una potencia de salida limitada
}

OscillatorBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón oscilador láser
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un condensador de pulsos integrado dispara un pulso de energía en el extremo del rayo cada 30 fotogramas
		El daño directo se reduce ligeramente, pero las ráfagas de área y el menor coste de maná compensan el fuego sostenido
		'''
}

ScorchBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón láser quemado
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una pico de plasma de alta entalpía prende fuego a los enemigos al entrar en contacto con el láser
		El daño directo del rayo es ligeramente menor, pero la combustión continuada compensa la pérdida de potencia directa
		'''
}

ReflectionBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón láser reflectante
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un prisma de diamante situado en el punto de impacto desvía parte de la energía hacia dos haces laterales
		El daño del haz principal aumenta, pero el enorme consumo de maná hace que el disparo sostenido resulte muy costoso
		'''
}

EchoOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor eco
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un elemento resonante situado al final del recorrido capta el eco de energía cuando un haz se extingue
		Cada vez que un haz se extingue, se generan tres subhaces autoguiados que se dispersan en abanico, compensando así el alcance reducido
		'''
}

FrostOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor escarchado
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una lente de enfoque criogénico inflige Quemadura por escarcha a los objetivos alcanzados
		La velocidad del rayo se reduce, pero el seguimiento es más estable, con bonificaciones a la penetración y a los golpes críticos
		'''
}

SingularityCoreModule: {
	DisplayName: Núcleo de singularidad
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un generador de microgravedad dirige continuamente el orbe hacia el enemigo más cercano
		El radio de la explosión se amplía considerablemente, pero el campo denso aumenta el coste de maná
		'''
}

ScrambleFieldModule: {
	DisplayName: Módulo de campo de combate
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una bobina de alta frecuencia dispara una microonda de choque alrededor del orbe cada 40 fotogramas mientras se carga
		La potencia del impacto se amplifica a cambio de un tiempo de carga más lento y un mayor consumo de maná
		'''
}

BraceStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata de soporte
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Si te quedas quieto sobre terreno firme durante aproximadamente un segundo, se despliega automáticamente un trípode hidráulico que te fija en modo torreta
		Mientras está desplegado: los rayos no se dispersan, su alcance y velocidad aumentan considerablemente, obtienen penetración adicional 
		y estabilización balística, además de un +8% de probabilidad de golpe crítico
		Si te mueves o te alejas del suelo, el equipo se pliega al instante; volver a desplegarlo en un plazo de 8 segundos mantiene el sistema hidráulico en funcionamiento
		y es mucho más rápido
		Llevarlo equipado de serie otorga una dispersión del -20% y una velocidad de ataque del -5%
		'''
}

LaunchStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata de lanzamiento
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un mecanismo de resorte sobrecargado dispara tres rayos autoguiados en forma de abanico en el instante en que se lanza el orbe
		La velocidad del orbe aumenta a medida que crece el coste de maná
		'''
}

SentinelGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Empuñadura centinela
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una empuñadura con sensor inteligente dispara automáticamente un rayo autoguiado hacia el enemigo más cercano cada 20 fotogramas mientras el orbe está en el aire
		La velocidad del orbe se reduce ligeramente y el coste de maná aumenta, pero el disparo lateral continuo lo compensa
		'''
}

ConductorGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Empuñadura conductora
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El material superconductor aumenta el alcance y el número de saltos de los saltos de arco en cadena
		Cada impacto va acompañado de una ráfaga de partículas de arco; el daño y el coste de maná aumentan ligeramente
		'''
}

PhantomFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco fantasmal
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una cavidad de fase cuántica teletransporta el rayo a 80 píxeles del enemigo más cercano cada 30 fotogramas
		Esquiva los obstáculos por completo; aumenta ligeramente el alcance y el daño del rayo a cambio de un mayor coste de maná
		'''
}

RecursiveFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco recursivo
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un chasis de bucle topológico vuelve a lanzar cada rayo desde la posición del jugador en su dirección original al morir
		El daño del rayo principal aumenta, pero su alcance se reduce; el eco tiene un daño menor y no se repite
		'''
}

ForkBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón de horquilla
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un prisma divisor interno bifurca cada haz en dos subhaces en ángulo cada 50 fotogramas
		Ligeros daños y penalización en el coste de maná
		'''
}

NullBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón nulo
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una cámara de borrado de datos reduce el daño casi a cero, pero otorga una perforación prácticamente ilimitada
		Los golpes inyectan una toxina virulenta que corroe al objetivo con el paso del tiempo
		'''
}

HelixBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón en espiral
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El visor de doble canal hace que dos rayos giren en espiral alrededor de un eje común
		La dispersión se reduce a cero; provoca un daño leve y una ligera penalización de velocidad; ofrece una gran sinergia con configuraciones de alta penetración
		'''
}

TargetPainterOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Pintor de objetivos
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un sistema de designación láser marca los objetivos alcanzados con un líquido corrosivo, lo que reduce su defensa
		Además, aumenta la potencia de los misiles autoguiados y la probabilidad de asestar un golpe crítico
		'''
}

StrobeOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor estroboscópico
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un modulador de cambio de fase alterna rápidamente el haz entre los estados de penetración de paredes y el estado sólido
		Tiene un 30% de probabilidad de confundir a los enemigos alcanzados; ofrece una pequeña bonificación a la penetración y a la velocidad
		'''
}

SniperOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor de francotirador
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Si mantienes el disparo con el punto de mira fijo, se activa el bloqueo; una línea guía de francotirador aparece gradualmente desde la boca del cañón
		Una vez cargado, tu siguiente disparo se convierte en un "Rayo perforador del cielo": provoca daño masivo, perforación total, e impacto instantáneo
		Disparar restablece el bloqueo; mover bruscamente la mira agota el progreso, aunque moverse con libertad no lo hace
		La velocidad y alcance del rayo es mejorado, a cambio de una cadencia de disparo más lenta y una capacidad de seguimiento reducida a cero
		'''
}

StormCellModule: {
	DisplayName: Célula tormentosa
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Durante la carga, lanza un rayo eléctrico autoguiado hacia el enemigo más cercano cada 25 fotogramas
		Carga más rápido y tiene mayor radio de explosión, pero con un mayor coste de maná
		'''
}

CryoCoreModule: {
	DisplayName: Núcleo helado
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una célula de energía sobreenfriada congela a todos los enemigos que se encuentren dentro del radio de la explosión del orbe
		Explosión ligeramente más grande, carga ligeramente más lenta
		'''
}

DarkMatterCoreModule: {
	DisplayName: Núcleo de materia oscura
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un campo de materia oscura atrae a los enemigos cercanos hacia el orbe durante su vuelo
		El orbe rastrea simultáneamente a los objetivos; el radio de la explosión se ha incrementado considerablemente
		Alto coste de maná
		'''
}

ErgonomicStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata ergonómica
	Tooltip:
		'''
		La culata se adapta a tus manos: el fuego sostenido sobre un objetivo (o más o menos en la misma dirección) desarrolla la memoria muscular
		Los niveles de destreza desbloquean beneficios crecientes: una dispersión menor, luego una cadencia de tiro más rápida y, 
		finalmente, la Unión Arma-Cuerpo con la barra al máximo.
		En el nivel de Unión, los impactos en el objetivo memorizado te devuelven un poco de maná, los rayos obtienen una corrección de puntería adicional
		y unas imágenes residuales rítmicas te siguen a ti y al arma
		Cambiar de objetivo o dejar de disparar hace que la memoria se desvanezca rápidamente.
		'''
}

ExtenderStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata extensora
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un riel ampliado proporciona a los rayos mayor alcance y velocidad de vuelo con un coste de daño mínimo
		Corte terminal: una vez que el rayo ha recorrido una distancia suficiente, su energía residual se despliega lateralmente en el mismo sitio,
		formando una hoja de luz perpendicular a su trayectoria, que barre un área en forma de abanico para infligir daño final
		Los rayos que se extinguen prematuramente por agotamiento de la penetración se convierten en una hoja más pequeña, cuyo tamaño varía en función de la distancia recorrida; las muertes a quemarropa no activan nada.
		En modo láser, mantén pulsado el rayo brevemente y, a continuación, suelta la tecla de ataque para realizar un corte transversal en el punto del cursor sobre la columna
		'''
}

StormStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata tormentosa
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El fuego continuo crea un campo de tormenta arremolinado a tu alrededor que se disipa cuando dejas de disparar
		Los proyectiles hostiles que se encuentran dentro del campo son desviados por el ciclón, describiendo una trayectoria curva a tu alrededor
		Cuando se llena el medidor de tormenta, un rayo cae desde arriba sobre los enemigos que se encuentran dentro del campo
		'''
}

VampireGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre vampírico
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un agarre bioeléctrico convierte una parte del daño infligido por el rayo en recuperación de salud
		Los disparos láser son más frecuentes, pero restauran menos salud por turno; resultan eficaces en combates prolongados
		'''
}

ChronalGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre crónico
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una bobina de retardo de fase ralentiza a los enemigos con cada impacto
		En combinación con una mejor capacidad de seguimiento, el fuego denso permite mantener un control de masas constante
		'''
}

CascadeGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre en cascada
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Cada 5 impactos, aparece un nodo en cascada que flota en el punto de impacto
		El nodo permanece unos 2 segundos y dispara 5 rayos autoguiados que persiguen a los enemigos cercanos
		Reduce ligeramente el daño base
		'''
}

MirrorFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco de espejo
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una cavidad de reflexión simétrica genera un rayo reflejo de 180 grados por cada rayo disparado
		Los rayos reflejos infligen menos daño; la cobertura bidireccional aumenta considerablemente la densidad de impactos
		'''
}

NullspaceFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco del espacio nulo
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un generador de grietas del vacío deja un eco de microexplosión a lo largo de la trayectoria del rayo cada 20 fotogramas
		Alcance ligeramente ampliado; penalización mínima de daño
		'''
}

OverkillFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco overkill
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un circuito de detección de overkill acumula una carga de overkill por cada muerte, hasta un máximo de 15; cada acumulación añade un 2% de daño.
		Las acumulaciones se van perdiendo con el tiempo: cuanto más rápido mates, más fuerte te harás.
		'''
}

GraviticBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón gravitacional
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una microsingularidad integrada atrae a los enemigos cercanos hacia cada rayo
		La dispersión y la capacidad de seguimiento se reducen a medida que aumenta el alcance; la velocidad inicial disminuye ligeramente
		'''
}

PrismaticBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón prismática
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los prismas de dispersión lanzan trazas RGB desde cada rayo, esparciendo fragmentos de color al impactar
		Añade un rayo adicional y una ventaja crítico a cambio de un ligero descenso en el daño y la dispersión
		'''
}

ConcussionBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon para conmociones cerebrales
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un amortiguador de sobrecarga provoca una pequeña onda de choque en el punto de impacto cada 5 golpes
		El daño por disparo y la dispersión se reducen, pero la velocidad de ataque se ve afectada
		'''
}

ObsidianBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañón de obsidiana
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los impactos tallan grietas de obsidiana en los objetivos; cuando se acumulan al máximo, estos se hacen añicos y se convierten en cristales volcánicos
		Las detonaciones de los orbes rompen prematuramente las grietas cercanas, lo que recompensa la presión constante sobre grupos de enemigos
		'''
}

LifebloomBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon floreciente
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los rayos lanzan brotes de vida parásitos que absorben el daño diferido y devuelven un poco de vida al portador
		Cuando el huésped muere, el brote se traslada a un enemigo cercano y sigue creciendo
		'''
}

MagmaVentBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon contuctor de magma
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los impactos y los haces dejan conductos de magma efímeros que erupcionan periódicamente en columnas de calor verticales
		Las condiciones del inframundo y del líquido a alta temperatura aceleran el ciclo de los conductos, lo que impide el acceso a la zona
		'''
}

CumulusBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon de cúmulos
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Las trayectorias de los rayos condensan nodos de nubes cargadas que se alimentan de los rayos SHPC y los orbes de carga cercanos
		Una vez llena, cada nube lanza tres rayos cortos de lluvia y relámpagos para proporcionar potencia de fuego posicional
		'''
}

MossboundBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon cubierto de musgo
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los rayos siembran manchas de musgo húmedo que ralentizan a los enemigos y se acumulan hasta formar una breve trampa de raíces
		Los orbes de carga voladores absorben el musgo cercano para aumentar la potencia de su explosión final
		'''
}

FrostfernBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon a prueba de heladas
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El primer golpe traza una veta de hielo detrás del objetivo, afectando con frío a los enemigos que se encuentren en su trayectoria
		Enlaza a los grupos mediante una geometría ramificada en forma de helecho, en lugar de limitarse a congelar a una sola víctima
		'''
}

SandstormBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon tempestad de arena
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Un disparo incesante hace avanzar una cortina de arena en movimiento, que desgasta a los enemigos y debilita los proyectiles hostiles
		Los rayos ganan penetración adicional, mientras que la absorción de maná aumenta para mantener la tormenta en movimiento
		'''
}

CoralReefBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon arrecife de coral
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los puntos de impacto generan anclas de coral que se unen formando líneas de arrecifes destructivas
		Las detonaciones de los orbes hacen que las anclas cercanas liberen ondas circulares sincronizadas
		'''
}

HiveBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cñaon colmena
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Al hacer clic izquierdo se rocía a los enemigos con feromonas; a continuación, la detonación de los orbes lanza abejas cibernéticas contra los objetivos marcados
		Coloca marcadores por todo el campo de batalla para que el enjambre se divida y cubra todo el terreno
		'''
}

MoondewBarrelModule: {
	DisplayName: Cañon de rocío lunar
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los rastros de los rayos condensan prismas de rocío que refractan los rayos posteriores en breves destellos derivados
		Las noches de luna llena o casi llena aumentan el límite máximo de refracción de cada prisma y el efecto resultante
		'''
}

CrosslinkOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor entrecruzado
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Al impactar, una unidad de enlace neural establece una conexión de datos entre el objetivo alcanzado y el enemigo más cercano
		Tanto el número de eslabones como el alcance de la cadena aumentan, con un ligero incremento del coste de maná
		'''
}

ZoomOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor de enfoque
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Una lente magnética de largo alcance impulsa los rayos con mayor velocidad y alcance, a costa de la velocidad de seguimiento y de ataque
		Los impactos a más de 600 píxeles activan un golpe incandescente adicional que aumenta en función de la distancia
		'''
}

PingOpticModule: {
	DisplayName: Visor de ping
	Tooltip: El sistema "Pintor de señales" aplica "Marcado para morir" al impactar y otorga una probabilidad de crítico adicional
}

CapacitorPulseModule: {
	DisplayName: Impulso de condensador
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Las densas pilas de condensadores emiten una detonación de micropulsos aproximadamente dos veces por segundo mientras se cargan
		Tanto el radio de la explosión como el tiempo de carga aumentan, y el coste de maná se incrementa
		'''
}

EntropyCoreModule: {
	DisplayName: Núcleo de entropía
	Tooltip:
		'''
		El orbe absorbe entropía de los enemigos cercanos mientras vuela
		Al detonar, provoca una onda de choque secundaria cuya intensidad depende de la entropía acumulada
		'''
}

ResonanceReactorModule: {
	DisplayName: Reactor de resonancia
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Emite un sonido de resonancia cada ~0,75 s mientras se carga
		La detonación provoca una onda de choque de resonancia adicional a los pies del jugador, que cubre las distancias en combate cuerpo a cuerpo
		'''
}

OverwatchStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata supervisora
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Si te quedas quieto, se acumulan cargas de Supervisor (máximo 5), que desaparecen rápidamente en cuanto te mueves
		Cada carga otorga un +2,5 % de daño y un +2 % de crítico; esta postura estoica reduce la velocidad de ataque y la dispersión
		'''
}

MomentumStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata de impulsos
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Moverte rápidamente aumenta las acumulaciones de Impulso (máximo 6), que desaparecen rápidamente en cuanto te detienes.
		Cada acumulación otorga un +5 % de velocidad de ataque y un +8 % de velocidad de disparo, al igual que en Supervisor
		'''
}

BulwarkStockModule: {
	DisplayName: Culata baluarte
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Sostener el SHPC proporciona una reducción moderada del daño
		La postura reforzada ralentiza ligeramente el tiempo de carga y reduce el coste de maná
		'''
}

CombatGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre de combate
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los golpes mortales con rayos o láser acumulan cargas de Combate (máximo 5)
		Cada carga otorga un +4% de velocidad de ataque y un +2% de daño; las cargas se pierden entre combates
		'''
}

TempestGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre tempestuoso
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Tras cada serie de golpes consecutivos, lanza una Ráfaga de tempestad: múltiples arcos de datos que se extienden alrededor del último impacto
		El daño por disparo se reduce y el coste de maná aumenta a cambio de una limpieza rítmica
		'''
}

AbsorberGripModule: {
	DisplayName: Agarre amortiguador
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Los impactos de rayos y láseres devuelven una parte del daño infligido en forma de maná
		A cambio, el daño por disparo disminuye ligeramente y el coste de maná base aumenta
		'''
}

HarmonicFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco armónico
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Cuando coexisten varios rayos, estos se unen entre sí mediante resonancia para infligir daño adicional
		Añade un rayo adicional a costa de una reducción del daño por disparo y un ligero aumento de la dispersión
		'''
}

ReplicatorFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco replicador
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Al desaparecer, el rayo genera un breve eco en el mismo lugar que sigue volando en la misma dirección que el rayo original
		El daño principal aumenta a medida que se reduce el alcance; el coste de maná también aumenta
		'''
}

ArchiveFrameModule: {
	DisplayName: Marco de archivo
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Acumula daño SHPC; cada vez que se supera el umbral, una explosión de Archivo detona a los pies del jugador
		El daño por disparo aumenta ligeramente, con un pequeño coste adicional de maná
		'''
}

CWRItem: {
	TemperatureText: Temperatura de combustión
	InternalStoredEnergy: Energía alamacenada
	BrutalWorldItemText: Exclusivo del Mundo Cruel
	BrutalRelicSeriesText: Reliquia cruel · exclusivo del Mundo Cruel
	LegendItemUpgradeDisable:
		'''
		Esta arma legendaria no se puede mejorar en el mundo actual.
		Vuelve a entrar en el mundo para eliminar esta restricción.
		'''
	ItemLegendOnMouseLang: Presiona 'Shift' para escuchar su historia...

	CWRItem: {
		TemperatureText: Temperatura de combustión
		InternalStoredEnergy:Energía alamacenada
		BrutalWorldItemText: Exclusivo del Mundo Cruel
		BrutalRelicSeriesText: Reliquia cruel · exclusivo del Mundo Cruel
		LegendItemUpgradeDisable:
			'''
			Esta arma legendaria no se puede mejorar en el mundo actual.
			Vuelve a entrar en el mundo para eliminar esta restricción.
			'''
		ItemLegendOnMouseLang: Presiona 'Shift' para escuchar su historia...
	}
}

RMagicConch: {
	DontUseMagicConch: Te está observando una criatura poderosa...

	RMagicConch: {
		DontUseMagicConch: Te está observando una criatura poderosa...
		DisplayName: Caracola mágica
		Tooltip: Escucha con atención y oirás el mar
	}
}

GraniteTome: {
	DisplayName: Libro de granito
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Recita un conjuro para reunir tres partículas de carga y, a continuación, lanza un abanico de tres orbes de energía de granito que se dirigen lentamente hacia el objetivo
		Al impactar, los orbes se hacen añicos y se convierten en fragmentos de cristal que persiguen al objetivo.
		'''
}

GraniteFlower: {
	DisplayName: Floración de granito
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Lanza una semilla de cristal que florece y se convierte en una flor de energía persistente allí donde cae
		La flor late tres veces, lanzando pétalos de cristal al enemigo más cercano
		Se marchita al romperse todos sus pétalos, lanzando fragmentos de cristal en todas direcciones
		'''
}

GraniteThrowingKnife: {
	DisplayName: Cuchillo arrojadizo de granito
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Lanza un cuchillo perforante que traza un arco azul tan afilado como una navaja
		Al impactar en un enemigo, se propaga una cadena de rayos en miniatura hacia otro enemigo cercano
		Se hace añicos en fragmentos de cristal al realizar su último impacto o al chocar contra el terreno
		'''
}

GraniteWalkingBoots: {
	DisplayName: Botas de senderismo de granito
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Aumenta considerablemente la velocidad al correr y la aceleración
		Las plantas de los pies se llenan de electricidad en el instante en que alcanzas la velocidad máxima
		A toda velocidad, las chispas crepitan bajo tus pies y unas estelas azules se prolongan tras de ti
		'''
}

MarbleClub: {
	DisplayName: Garrote de mármol
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hace un golpe descendente lento y aplastante con un enorme empuje hacia atrás
		Los impactos siempre petrifican brevemente a los enemigos, dejándolos inmovilizados y lentos
		Al golpear el suelo, se desata una onda de choque de mármol a plena potencia y una oleada de polvo
		Los golpes en el aire solo provocan una onda de choque más débil
		'''
}

MarbleHuntingKnife: {
	DisplayName: Cuchillo arrojadizo de mármol
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hace tajos rápidos alternos
		Cada tercer golpe hace remate más amplio, lanzándose hacia delante y esparciendo fragmentos de mármol
		'''
}

MarbleDisc: {
	DisplayName: Disco de mármol
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Lanza un disco giratorio que rebota entre los enemigos y las paredes
		Cada rebote contra un nuevo objetivo dora el disco, lo que aumenta su daño en un 10%, hasta un máximo del 30%
		Una vez agotados los rebotes, vuelve volando a tu mano; pueden volar hasta dos a la vez
		'''
}

MarblePebble: {
	DisplayName: Guijarro de mármol
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Lanza una piedra con una velocidad infinita que rebota una vez en el suelo
		Inflige un daño mucho mayor a los enemigos con mucha vida máxima
		Al impactar contra un enemigo colosal, estalla en una luz dorada y produce un estruendo capaz de hacer vibrar las rocas
		'''
}

MarbleShield: {
	DisplayName: Égida de mármol
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Aumenta ligeramente el empuje hacia atrás en los ataques cuerpo a cuerpo
		Tres fragmentos de mármol que giran en órbita forman una guardia de piedra, que absorbe un golpe entrante y se hace añicos cuando está lista
		Pulsa [KEY] para levantar la guardia: un bloqueo perfecto anula el golpe, aplasta los proyectiles cercanos y lanza de vuelta las cuchillas de piedra
		Un bloqueo perfecto otorga un aumento del 10% en el daño cuerpo a cuerpo durante 5 segundos
		'''
}

MarbleBalloon: {
	DisplayName: Globo de mármol
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Pulsa Abajo mientras estás en el aire para realizar un aterrizaje en picado; cuanto más larga sea la caída, 
		más fuerte y amplia será la onda de choque del aterrizaje
		Anula el daño por caída
		'''
}

MarbleinaBottle: {
	DisplayName: Nube de mármol en una botella
	Tooltip: Otorga un segundo salto potente y enérgico; mantén pulsado Saltar para elevarte más alto
}

TestItem: {
	DisplayName: Ítem de pruebas
	Tooltip: ""
}

OniMeiRubbingHigekiri: {
	DisplayName: Higekiri
	Tooltip: Wounded foes take far more, and a personal kill refunds stance; weapon damage -2%
	Origin: The night of the clan's test cut, this blade took the head and the beard beneath the chin in one stroke — the whiskers were found still clinging to the edge. The old name Higekiri, the Beard-Cutter, was earned that night
	Power:
		'''
		Beard-Cutter: once a foe drops below 35% life, hits from the blade itself start scaling with the wound
		The thinner its life, the bigger the bonus: up to +60% on regular foes, up to +45% on bosses
		Finishing it yourself also refunds 8 stance, once per action
		'''
	Burden: Weapon damage -2%. While a foe is still healthy, this edge is duller than the original name
}

OniKeikoRune: {
	DisplayName: Keiko Rune
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Use it to open the Onikiri lesson from the beginning, or use it again mid-lesson to put the lesson away
		Left with you when the opening lesson is declined; the rune is not consumed and may be used again
		'''
	NeedBlade: Onikiri is not in your bag, so the rune has no lesson to open
	Closed: The lesson is put away; use the rune again to reopen
	NotNow: Something else holds the stage right now
}

OniMeiRubbingOnikiri: {
	DisplayName: Onikiri
	Tooltip: The original inscription. Nothing granted, nothing charged
	Origin: Watanabe no Tsuna carried it at the bridge of Ichijo-Modoribashi and cut an oni's arm clean off; the demon fled and never dared return for it. A blade that had cut an oni was named Onikiri for the feat, and the name has stayed nailed to the tang ever since
	Power: The original inscription. Everything this blade already has stays exactly as it is
	Burden: None
}

OniMeiRubbingShishinoko: {
	DisplayName: Shishi-no-ko
	Tooltip: Land all five beats and the fifth adds two crossing waves; beat interval +2%
	Origin: One night, left by its master's pillow, the blade roared on its own — a lion's cry, heard through the whole house. The master renamed it Shishi-no-ko, the Lion's Cub, and set the name in gold inlay to give that one roar its due
	Power:
		'''
		Lion's Roar: run all five combo beats through without a dash or a big art cutting in, and the fifth beat closes like a lion's jaws
		Two waves cross out of it, each for 22% of a blade hit
		'''
	Burden: Combo beat interval +2%. A roar has to be drawn in first, so the blade runs a touch slower
}

OniMeiRubbingTomokiri: {
	DisplayName: Tomokiri
	Tooltip: Dash-cancelling a combo leaves a Guilt slash behind; damage taken +6% while held
	Origin: Two treasured blades of the clan were tested edge against edge, and this one cut its companion clean in two. The fault was chiseled in as its name — Tomokiri, the Friend-Cutter — and its temper has run violent ever since
	Power:
		'''
		Guilt-Echo: when a Kamui flash step cuts your combo short, the interrupted swing stays behind
		It bites down on its own a moment later for 35% of a blade hit
		'''
	Burden:
		'''
		While you hold this blade, damage you take is +6%
		Every echo adds one layer of Guilt, up to three, and each layer makes your next dash cost 4 more vigor
		Land the Zanshin strike after a dash and the whole debt is paid off at once
		'''
}

OniMeiRubbingKazehi: {
	DisplayName: Kaze-hi
	Tooltip: Dashes cost 15% less vigor and Sakura Flight 20% less; ink brand damage -20%
	Origin: The edge-setter cut this groove long and straight, calling it a lane left open for the wind. Swing, and the wind arrives first — by the time you hear it, the blade is already back
	Power: Wind-Rider: Kamui flash step vigor cost -15%, Sakura Flight drain -20%
	Burden: Ink brands left by dashes deal -20% damage. This groove was cut for lightness, not for slaughter
}

OniMeiRubbingChihi: {
	DisplayName: Chi-hi
	Tooltip: Landing hits gives vigor back; natural regen -35%
	Origin: Other grooves are opened to lighten the blade; not this one. The edge-setter was blunt when he handed the sword over: this channel is for blood — the faster it runs, the faster your breath comes back
	Power:
		'''
		Bloodletting: the first hit of each combo beat returns 1 extra vigor
		Every Zanshin strike after a dash returns 4 extra
		'''
	Burden: Natural regen -35%, and you wait 0.3s longer before it starts back up after spending. No blood on the edge, little breath returned
}

OniMeiRubbingFudo: {
	DisplayName: Fudo
	Tooltip: Take a hit mid-art and spend stance to soften it; stance gain -15%
	Origin: The carver followed the brushwork of the seed syllable Kan and brought the Immovable One, flames at his back, onto the side of the blade. This deity's whole office is steadiness: whatever comes, he sits unmoved
	Power:
		'''
		Immovable: get hit during a Zanshin strike, Annihilating Flash, or Finale Slash, the arts you cannot pull out of, and the Immovable One takes it for you
		It spends 20 stance, leaves that hit at 65% damage and 25% knockback, then rests 2.5s
		'''
	Burden: Everyday stance gain -15%, since the guarding strength is skimmed off your build-up. Dismemberment backlash is never shielded
}

OniMeiRubbingKurikara: {
	DisplayName: Kurikara
	Tooltip: An execution banks three dragonfire layers, one spent per full combo; vigor cap -10%
	Origin: Carved on the blade is Kurikara the dragon king: a black dragon coiled around a sword, jaws open to swallow the point. It is an old subject of blade carving, with gold still set in the seams of the scales
	Power:
		'''
		Dragon-Coil: after an execution the blade lights three layers of dragonfire, good for ten seconds
		Every time you finish a full five-beat combo, the fifth beat burns one layer into a coiling slash for 50% of a blade hit
		'''
	Burden: Vigor cap -10%. Where the dragon coils, the breath runs narrow
}

OniMeiRubbingTessetsu: {
	DisplayName: Tessetsu
	Tooltip: First hit of each beat deals +25% to steel and machines; weapon damage -10%
	Origin: Someone inspected the blade and sneered: big name, edge like a length of raw iron. The smith took no offense and chiseled the heckle into the tang as it was — raw iron, then; iron against iron shows the true work
	Power: Iron-Cut: the first hit of each combo beat deals +25% damage to steel and machine foes, the ones that throw sparks when you cut them
	Burden: Weapon damage -10%. On flesh it really does feel like a length of dull iron
}

OniMeiRubbingKyushu: {
	DisplayName: Kyushu
	Tooltip: Heads only, and wounded heads harder than Higekiri manages; weapon damage -3%
	Origin: Some blades take a new name for every fine head they cut, and enjoy the parade each time. This inscription's bearer wanted none of it: heads fall as before, the name stays as before — a blade that cuts clean needs no new name to frighten anyone
	Power:
		'''
		Head-Hunt: the bonus only counts heads, or foes that have no separate segments to begin with
		Once it drops below 35% life your hits start scaling with the wound, and the thinner its life the bigger the bonus
		Up to +85% on regular foes, up to +60% on bosses
		'''
	Burden: Weapon damage -3%. Bodies, tails, and other segments do not count as a head
}

OniMeiRubbingIkiai: {
	DisplayName: Ikiai
	Tooltip: A full combo's fifth beat throws a sword arc along your aim; beat interval +4%
	Origin: Old swordsmen say that in a long standoff the two sides' breathing locks together, and whoever closes that breath first lands first. This inscription records the craft: hold it in, match the beat, drop the blade
	Power: Breath-Wave: finish a full five-beat combo and the fifth beat throws a curved sword arc along your aim for 55% of a blade hit, cutting up to three foes before it breaks up
	Burden: Combo beat interval +4%
}

OniMeiRubbingKyoko: {
	DisplayName: Kyoko
	Tooltip: Back off to bank a cut, then close in and it lands harder; hammering up close blurs your focus
	Origin: A blade tester roared into an empty valley and no echo came back — with no one around, the whole breath pressed itself back into the blade. This carving records that pent-up cry
	Power:
		'''
		Hollow-Roar: keep 16 tiles clear of enemies for 1.5s and the blade banks a cut for you
		Your next hit within 16 tiles deals +25%; hits landed further out do not spend it, so the banked cut keeps
		When the blade idles it rings on its own: 1.5s without landing a hit, or with nothing near you, it slows foes within 20 tiles for 0.4s every 1.5s
		'''
	Burden: Four close-range hits inside 0.6s blur your focus for 0.4s, and close-range damage drops 5% for that window
}

OniMeiRubbingKarikiri: {
	DisplayName: Karikiri
	Tooltip: A dash leaves a decoy that eats one hit for you; 4s before you get another
	Origin: A student copied his master's stance ten parts in ten, and the master gave one verdict: too alike — alike enough to read false at a glance. This inscription records that false body: however well it stands, it is only a shadow that takes the blade in your stead
	Power:
		'''
		False Body: starting a Kamui flash step leaves a frozen-pose decoy standing for 1.5s
		Anything that comes at you in that window, foe or projectile, is taken by the decoy instead
		Once it has spent itself, you wait 4s before you can leave another
		'''
	Burden:
		'''
		While the decoy stands, damage taken and dash cost are both +12%
		For 1s after it shatters, damage taken is +18%
		A decoy that simply runs out of time does not count as shattered
		'''
}

OniMeiRubbingMokukiri: {
	DisplayName: Mokukiri
	Tooltip: Finish a paid normal dash and the next cut deals +35%; a whiff spends it too
	Origin: The instant a flash step runs its course, everything around falls quiet. Old swordsmen know the next cut out of that silence is the heaviest. The name says it plainly: the silent cut
	Power: Silent-Kill: for 0.75s after a paid normal flash step runs its course, your next combo swing or Zanshin strike deals +35%
	Burden: A whiff spends it just the same, and dashing again clears it. Free execution dashes never bank it
}

OniMeiRubbingKumokiri: {
	DisplayName: Kumo-kiri
	Tooltip: Three cuts pin a web; closing it cuts everything inside; regen -25% while anchors stand
	Origin: Minamoto no Raiko lay sick in bed when a tsuchigumo, disguised as a priest, came to bind him in silk. He snatched up the blade, cut the threads and wounded the beast, and the next day followed the blood trail and destroyed its nest. The blade has been called Kumo-kiri, the Spider-Cutter, ever since
	Power:
		'''
		Ink-Silk: when the blade itself lands a hit, it pins a silk anchor at the cut point for 4s
		Spread them out: the same foe gives no second anchor within 0.4s, and two anchors need roughly six tiles between them
		The third anchor strings an ink-silk triangle that sags, then snaps toward its centre, cutting every foe it sweeps for 90% of a blade hit and binding them 1s
		After it closes, 1.5s pass before you can weave again
		'''
	Burden: While any anchor still stands, natural regen -25%. An anchor left to expire wastes the cut that set it
	DeedHint: Slay thirty arachnids — spiders, blood crawlers, sand scorpions, any eight-legged wall-crawler counts. Cut down enough and the blade learns that stench by itself
}

OniMeiRubbingOnimaru: {
	DisplayName: Oni-maru
	Tooltip: Stand still and the blade flies off to cut on its own; you have no blade while it is out
	Origin: Onimaru Kunitsuna, of the Five Great Swords. Its master was tormented night after night by a small oni in his dreams, until one night the blade toppled from its stand on its own and severed the oni head carved on the brazier's leg — the nightmares ended on the spot. The man does not move; the blade moves by itself
	Power:
		'''
		Self-Cut: stand nearly still for 1s and the blade goes on standby
		From then on it spends 10 of your vigor every 1.5s to fly at a foe within 40 tiles, cut for 140% of a blade hit, and return to the sheath
		'''
	Burden: The blade is out of your hands for the whole flight, so no combo, no flash step, no Sakura Flight. With nothing nearby it will not launch
	DeedHint: Hold the blade and stand dead still for ten seconds, without stepping away even when a hit lands — hold your ground, and the blade moves for you that once
}

OniMeiRubbingRaikiri: {
	DisplayName: Rai-kiri
	Tooltip: The fifth beat and the big arts call lightning under open sky; beat interval +6%, nothing indoors
	Origin: Tachibana Dosetsu was sheltering under a tree when a bolt of lightning came down on his head; he drew and cut back at it, and lived. The blade has been called Raikiri, the Thunder-Cutter, ever since
	Power:
		'''
		Thunder-Call: when the fifth beat, a Zanshin strike, Annihilating Flash, or Finale Slash lands and there is open sky overhead, a bolt drops from the top of the world
		The bolt deals 70% of a blade hit, and in a thunderstorm one strike can call up to three
		'''
	Burden: Combo beat interval +6%, sunny days included, because the wind-up is paid either way. Blocked overhead or underground, no bolt falls
	DeedHint: Slay a boss-tier foe in a storm under open sky, and the edge learns the bolt
}

OniMeiRubbingNuekiri: {
	DisplayName: Nue-kiri
	Tooltip: Finish a combo airborne and the fifth beat becomes a ground slam; no dashing for 0.7s after landing
	Origin: A nue coiled over the palace roof at night, and Minamoto no Yorimasa's arrow brought it down out of the clouds. The finishing cut, dealt the instant it hit the ground, drove straight down along the fall — and that plunge is what this inscription remembers
	Power:
		'''
		Nue-Dive: finish a full combo at least three tiles off the ground and the fifth beat stops swinging sideways, diving at the floor instead
		The landing opens a shock ring about 12 tiles across for 120% of a blade hit, and drags nearby foes toward the impact
		'''
	Burden: No flash steps for about 0.7s after you land. Fought close to the ground, the fifth beat stays an ordinary fifth beat
	DeedHint: At night, rise thirty tiles above the ground and slay a flying foe, and the blade learns that plunge
}

OniMeiRubbingKamihi: {
	DisplayName: Kami-hi
	Tooltip: Dashing through a foe drops a paper cutout; cutting the paper hits the foe; dashes cost more while paper stands
	Origin: A master paper-mounter's cut leaves paper as paper and shadow as shadow. This groove studied that hand: passing through a foe, it trims their silhouette off and leaves it standing where it was — while the paper stands, the account can be settled against it
	Power:
		'''
		Paper-Effigy: dashing through a foe leaves a paper cutout of it where you land, good for 7s, two on the field at most
		Cutting that paper deals 80% of a blade hit straight to the foe itself
		It also opens a wound on the foe for 1.5s, and your hits land 12% harder while that wound is open
		'''
	Burden: Dash vigor cost +12% while any effigy stands
	DeedHint: Sever twenty omokage paper silhouettes in the Ura world, and the hand learns how paper is cut
}

OniMeiRubbingSorahi: {
	DisplayName: Sora-hi
	Tooltip: One extra dash off the ground and double regen; the first 0.75s after landing gives nothing back
	Origin: The master who opened this groove kept an odd theory: breath is like people — the moment its feet touch the ground, it turns lazy. So he cut the blade featherlight, to keep you in the air a little longer; while you float, the breath comes looking for you
	Power:
		'''
		Air-Groove: natural regen doubles while both feet are off the ground, and you get one extra dash
		An air dash that runs out leaves you hovering at its endpoint for half a second
		'''
	Burden: Natural regen drops to zero for 0.75s after you land, and dashing on the ground costs 10% more vigor
	DeedHint: Stay off the ground for fifteen straight seconds and land at least five blade hits meanwhile, and the groove learns to float
}

OniMeiRubbingKagamihi: {
	DisplayName: Kagami-hi
	Tooltip: A dash endpoint stands a paper mirror that copies your next cut; weapon damage -5%
	Origin: Mirror polishers all know it: the figure in the glass looks synchronized, but always runs half a beat behind. The one who opened this groove wanted exactly that half beat — let the one in the mirror deal your follow-up cut. Late, but it arrives
	Power:
		'''
		Mirror-Echo: the endpoint of a Kamui flash step stands a paper mirror for 2s
		The next time you cut, the figure in the mirror repeats that same cut for 45% of a blade hit, then shatters
		'''
	Burden: Weapon damage -5%. The copy swings from wherever the mirror stands, so whether it connects is on you
	DeedHint: Finish a mimic with the Zanshin strike — Calamity's counterfeit counts among the imitators too
}

OniMeiRubbingAmahi: {
	DisplayName: Ama-hi
	Tooltip: Sakura Flight drips ink that pools and binds where it lands; Sakura drain +15%
	Origin: The gutter under the eaves is also called an amahi, a rain channel. The edge-setter cut this groove with the eaves in mind: rain you catch should not run off for nothing — fly on, and let it drip onto whoever waits under the blade
	Power:
		'''
		Ink-Rain: while cruising in Sakura Flight, a bead of ink drops every 0.1s for 12% of a blade hit
		Beads spread into puddles where they land, and foes that step in are bound for half a second
		'''
	Burden: Sakura Flight drain +15%. Carrying rain the whole way costs
	DeedHint: Fly Sakura Flight through the rain for ten straight seconds; petals must soak through before water will stay
}

OniMeiRubbingTsuzurihi: {
	DisplayName: Tsuzuri-hi
	Tooltip: Ink brands from one dash cut lines between each other; a lone brand deals -30%
	Origin: Tsuzuri is the bookbinder's stitch: one needle, one hole, and when the thread pulls tight the loose pages become a book. The one who opened this groove uses ink brands for stitch holes: string the marks together, and they close into a line
	Power: Mark-Stitch: ink brands from the same dash all go off together and cut lines between one another, each line for 35% of a blade hit
	Burden: A lone ink brand deals -30%. Catch only one foe per dash and this groove is a pure loss
	DeedHint: Pierce six different foes in one dash, and the marks stitch
}

OniMeiRubbingBonsho: {
	DisplayName: Bonsho
	Tooltip: Hold full stance without a Finale and the blade tolls itself; half your stance buys a ring of control
	Origin: A temple bell waits for someone to strike it; the one carved on this blade does not. The carver put it plainly: build your stance full and sit on it, and the bell will let it go for you
	Power:
		'''
		Bell-Toll: hold full stance for 3s without releasing Finale Slash and the blade tolls on its own
		Foes within 30 tiles each take 60% of a blade hit and are bound 1.5s, and your stance drops to 50
		'''
	Burden: Once the bell rings, that Finale is gone. Full stance forces you to pick one
	DeedHint: Bring a boss down without using Annihilating Flash or Finale Slash the whole fight — knock the bell down just like that
}

OniMeiRubbingHannya: {
	DisplayName: Hannya
	Tooltip: Drop low and the mask turns demon: heavier hits and lifesteal; frail while it is out, duller before it turns
	Origin: The hannya mask of Noh plays the instant a woman's grudge turns her face into a demon's. The carver set that mask into the steel: push a person to the very edge, and the face turns over on its own
	Power:
		'''
		Mask-Shift: below 35% of your own life the mask turns demon, blade damage +20%, and every hit restores 0.5% of your max life
		While the demon face is out, every third hit brings up a mask that bites for 50% of a blade hit
		'''
	Burden: Damage taken +15% while the demon face is out. In maiden form, weapon damage -4%
	DeedHint: Slay a boss while your own life sits below one tenth, and the mask can turn
}

OniMeiRubbingKaresansui: {
	DisplayName: Karesansui
	Tooltip: Plant your feet to rake a sand garden that stays put, cutting and feeding stance
	Origin: A garden master raises mountains and seas with nothing but sand and stone — not one drop of water. The carver cut that raked pattern into the blade, saying that a swordsman who stands firm enough can rake a sand garden underfoot with his blade's edge
	Power:
		'''
		Sand-Garden: stand nearly still for 1.5s and a sand field about 20 tiles across is raked at your feet, lasting 5s
		The field cuts every half second for 18% of a blade hit
		While you stand inside your own field, stance gain +30%
		'''
	Burden: You have to plant first, and moving clears what you have built up
	DeedHint: Hold one spot for thirty seconds of combat without taking a hit, and the sand can be raked
}

OniMeiRubbingSenju: {
	DisplayName: Senju
	Tooltip: Six ghost arms join the Finale Slash freeze; afterwards vigor zeroes and dashing is locked 3s
	Origin: The Thousand-Armed Kannon offers one hand to each soul it ferries. The carver cut the thousand hands into the blade and set its rule: every one the Finale sends off must have a hand there to receive them
	Power: Thousand-Arms: during the Finale Slash freeze, six sword-bearing ghost arms rise behind you and cut with it, each for 30% of a blade hit
	Burden: After the Finale your vigor drops to zero and you cannot flash step for 3s
	DeedHint: Send off eight different bosses with the Finale Slash, one hand for each name
}

OniMeiRubbingKogehi: {
	DisplayName: Koge-hi
	Tooltip: Dashes leave up to five burns along the whole path; weapon damage -4%
	Origin: The master who opened this groove lived by the lava shallows and had seen too many people who never watch their feet. This groove, he said, is cut for stepping clear of the heat: you run through, and the burn stays on the ground behind you — for whoever gives chase
	Power:
		'''
		Scorch-Trail: a Kamui flash step leaves up to five burns spread along its full path, each burning 1.5s
		A foe standing in one is scorched every half second for 14% of a blade hit
		A new burn dropped within two tiles of an old one just refreshes it
		'''
	Burden: Weapon damage -4%; make the difference back with the burns your footwork lays down
}

OniMeiRubbingKanhi: {
	DisplayName: Kan-hi
	Tooltip: Let the blade go cold and natural regen runs 2.25x; dash and Sakura costs +8%
	Origin: A long bench sits by the sword shop's door, and the master rests there listening to the street once the work is done. People must learn to rest, he says: quiet the ears, and the breath returns quicker. This groove is that bench
	Power: Quiet-Breath: after two seconds without cutting anything, natural regen runs at 2.25x
	Burden: Dash and Sakura Flight costs +8%. Breath earned in the quiet is repaid in motion
}

OniMeiRubbingTodohi: {
	DisplayName: Todo-hi
	Tooltip: Hits glue foes down for 0.6s; dashes take 0.1s longer to come back
	Origin: This groove came out of a strange quench: the edge drags sticky through flesh, and whatever takes the cut stalls a step. The edge-setter never called it a flaw — it is the other one that sticks, not you
	Power: Ink-Bound: a hit from the blade itself glues the foe down for 0.6s, dropping regular movement to 88% and boss movement to 96%
	Burden: Dashes take 0.1s longer to come back around. Ink-Bound and Numbed do not stack on the same foe, only the stronger one applies
}

OniMeiRubbingShiorihi: {
	DisplayName: Shiori-hi
	Tooltip: Finish one foe and the edge prunes the most wounded one nearby; natural regen -10%
	Origin: A gardener prunes by one rule: once the shears are out, take the wilted stems in the same pass and spare yourself a second trip. The one who opened this groove used to be a gardener
	Power:
		'''
		Petal-Prune: when your blade finishes a foe, it looks 15 tiles out from where that foe fell
		It picks another foe under half life, chases it down, and prunes for 25% of a blade hit
		Finding nobody starts no cooldown; a successful prune rests 0.75s
		'''
	Burden: Natural regen -10%. A Zanshin strike that hits nothing costs 2 extra vigor. Kills made by the pruning blade never set off another
}

OniMeiRubbingShiohi: {
	DisplayName: Shio-hi
	Tooltip: Swing on the tide for vigor and a heavier Zanshin; off-beat combos come out dull
	Origin: The edge-setter grew up by the sea and whets blades to the rhythm of the tide. The tide rises and falls, he says, and so does a man's breath: a cut made on the rising tide, the sea repays
	Power:
		'''
		Tide-Beat: a tide head runs under the vigor stroke on a 0.8s cycle, and the 0.2s at its crest is the on-tide window
		Combos started on the tide return 3 vigor on their first hit, and an on-tide Zanshin strike deals +8%
		'''
	Burden: Off-tide combos deal -3%. The tide is read the moment you press, so catching it on the hit does not count
}

OniMeiRubbingShibori: {
	DisplayName: Shibori
	Tooltip: Dashing through a foe or eating a hit mid-art numbs whatever touched you; stance gain -15%
	Origin: A numbed hand must not let go of the grip — that is the first year of sword school. The master who cut this carving turned the lesson around: numb me by one measure, and whatever touched me goes numb by ten
	Power:
		'''
		Numb-Counter: dashing through a foe numbs it outright
		Take contact damage during an art you cannot pull out of and you may spend 15 stance to leave that hit at 85% and numb whatever landed it, then rest 1.5s
		A numbed foe moves slower for 0.75s, down to 90% for regular foes and 98% for bosses, and its contact damage drops 10%
		'''
	Burden: Everyday stance gain -15%
}

OniMeiRubbingChinmei: {
	DisplayName: Chinmei
	Tooltip: Hostile projectile damage -12% and knockback -65%; stance gain -15%
	Origin: Arrows and stones fill a battlefield, and one ringing of the ears is enough to panic a man. The old soldier who cut this inscription left a single line: steady yourself first, stand firm, then move — what flies at you will hurt less
	Power: Quell: hostile projectiles that hit you deal -12% damage, and their knockback is left at 35%
	Burden: Stance gain -15%. In a pure melee scrap this carving mostly sits idle
}

OniMeiRubbingAshidome: {
	DisplayName: Ashidome
	Tooltip: Plant for 0.75s and your next big art or fifth beat deals +25%
	Origin: Every fencing master opens the first lesson the same way: stop swaying on your feet. Planted feet hold strength, and held strength gives the strike its weight. This inscription keeps that first lesson for you
	Power: Planted-Step: stand nearly still for 0.75s to bank a cut, and your next fifth beat, Zanshin strike, Annihilating Flash, or Finale Slash deals +25%
	Burden: The bank is spent the moment the art starts, whiff included. Moving clears it
}

OniMeiRubbingYoen: {
	DisplayName: Yoen
	Tooltip: Executions leave one patch of embers on the ground, never more than one; vigor cap -5%
	Origin: After a forge is banked for the night, the warmth in the chamber keeps till morning. The edge-setter borrowed that rule for the blade: the fire is out, the heat is not
	Power:
		'''
		Ember-Field: an execution leaves a field of embers at the focus, burning 3s
		The same foe is scorched every 0.75s for 16% of a blade hit
		There is only ever one field; another execution moves it somewhere new
		'''
	Burden: Vigor cap -5%. While the embers are still burning, dashes cost 10% more vigor
}

ScrapBeacon: {
	DisplayName: Scrap Beacon
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons the Scrap Commander at night
		"Scrap always answers to its foreman"
		'''
}

GaolCellKey: {
	DisplayName: Deep Gaol Cell Key
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Builds the Deep Gaol cell on the spot and seats a dormant skull on the altar (test item)
		Approach the altar to wake it; during the fight both doorways are sealed by pale-pink energy bars
		Defeat the Deep Gaol Wraith to snuff the cell for good; a wraith that escapes goes dormant again after a few seconds
		"One turn of the key, and the walls remember their shape"
		'''
	BuiltHint: The cell has been raised. The dormant skull on the altar is waiting for you to come closer.
}

RustedGaolIrons: {
	DisplayName: Rusted Gaol Irons
	Tooltip:
		'''
		3 defense and immunity to knockback
		Briefly boosts movement speed after taking damage
		"The cell number inside the cuff has been worn smooth"
		'''
}

UndrownedShackleCharm: {
	DisplayName: Sunken Shackle Band
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Water no longer slows you down; grants the ability to swim
		Greatly extends underwater breathing time
		"The anchor sank. The man kept breathing"
		'''
}

GaolAnchorWeapon: {
	DisplayName: Gaol Anchor
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hurls a great anchor; while pinned into a wall, its chain becomes a damaging line
		"Execution tools do not retire"
		'''
}

SumpPearl: {
	DisplayName: Sump Pearl
	Tooltip:
		'''
		A matte pearl curdled from gaol water in a convict's bones
		The undead market accepts these
		'''
}

FloodGalleryKey: {
	DisplayName: Flood Gallery Key
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Builds the flood gallery on the spot and seats the anchored convict (test item)
		"The depth scale on the wall is his heartbeat chart"
		'''
	Placed: The Flood Gallery has been raised on the spot. To wake him, stand on the valve dais to the left and hold your ground.
}

ProofSealCharm: {
	DisplayName: Proofing Seal
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Trap projectiles deal 25% less damage and have a 15% chance to misfire
		"Stamped goods pass every mechanism unharassed"
		'''
	Misfire: Misfire
}

OverseerLogger: {
	DisplayName: Overseer's Logbook
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Grants danger sense; nearby traps and mechanisms are laid bare
		"It keeps the duty roster of every dart port"
		'''
}

ProofingHallKey: {
	DisplayName: Proofing Hall Key
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Builds the proofing hall on the spot and hangs the dust-caked rig (test item)
		"The inspection bell still rings"
		'''
	Placed: The Proofing Hall has been raised on the spot. To start the inspection, stand on the check-in dais to the left and hold still until the shift bell finishes counting.
}

WheezingWyrm: {
	DisplayName: Wheezing Wyrm
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hold to breathe a stream of dragonfire
		The old head has seen better days, and needs a few smoky coughs before it catches
		Sustained breathing stokes the throat ever hotter, from dull red all the way to searing blue
		Brighter flame burns hotter; blue flame deals the highest damage and ignites hellfire
		"Not quite dead, just an old smoker clearing its throat"
		'''
}

Abyssrend: {
	DisplayName: Abyssrend
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Left-click alternates tip thrusts and side cuts; each strike tears off a homing ocean undercurrent
		Right-click stirs an abyssal undertow that drags foes ahead of you onto the pincer, then slams them into the nearby ground, detonating a cavitation burst
		Foes caught by the slam or the burst sink into abyssal pressure, severely slowing them
		"It remembers the sound the deep makes when it breaks things"
		'''
}

SneezingWyrm: {
	DisplayName: Sneezing Wyrm
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Rapidly fires searing wyrmstrike rounds
		Sustained fire stokes the barrel hotter, pushing the tracers from orange toward blue-white
		With every gathered breath, the wyrm huffs a weaving, seeking bolt of dragonbreath down the line of fire
		Smoke tickles the old snout into intermittent sneezes that vent thick fumes to the side
		"Don't stand on its sneezing side"
		'''
}

TiroFinale: {
	DisplayName: Tiro Finale
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Benefits from both ranged and magic damage bonuses
		Firing consumes ammo and mana, weaving a golden phantom musket into the formation orbiting you with every shot
		While you hold fire, the formation takes turns aiming at your cursor, each musket ringing once before dissolving into light
		Right click to condense at least four phantom muskets into a great cannon and play the finale
		"Mind your manners, and make the curtain call magnificent"
		'''
}

Everdeep: {
	DisplayName: Everdeep
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Fires a ring of pressurized abyssal water
		The ring pierces through foes, coasts a short way, then curls back to strike again
		Hits build abyssal resonance, counted by the droplets orbiting the tome
		At full resonance, a giant maelstrom erupts from the ground beneath the victim
		"The deep does not part for you; it closes behind you"
		'''
}

Deepclaw: {
	DisplayName: Deepclaw
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons an abyssal lobster to fight for you
		The lobster lunges at enemies with snapping pincer strikes
		Every third pincer hit, it rears back and detonates a cavitation snap
		The snap deals area damage and drags enemies toward its center
		"What lives below never loosens its grip"
		'''
}

Undertow: {
	DisplayName: Undertow
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Turns any arrow into an abyssal spine
		When a spine strikes an enemy, its wake collapses into a small cavitation bubble that bursts again
		Hold right click to charge; release at full draw to loose a depth-pressure spine at 3x damage
		The heavy spine pierces everything and drags enemies toward its path
		When it finally stops, it detonates a cavitation implosion
		"The sea does not push you away; it takes you in"
		'''
}

TideReaper: {
	DisplayName: Tide Reaper
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hurls a spinning abyssal scythe that boomerangs back to you
		In flight it flings tide crescents that hunt nearby enemies
		Right click to throw a vortex anchor: the scythe pins ahead and spins into a maelstrom
		The maelstrom drags enemies inward and flings crescents faster before returning
		"When the tide goes out, only bones are left on the shore"
		'''
}

SeaShrimpShell: {
	DisplayName: Crystal Shrimp Shell
	Tooltip:
		'''
		A hardened carapace shed by the Abyssal Crystal Shrimp
		Essential crafting material for the abyssal weapon series
		"Hold it to your ear, and the trench still murmurs"
		'''
}

DeepcrystalWarhelm: {
	DisplayName: Deepcrystal Warhelm
	Tooltip:
		'''
		18% increased melee damage and 10% melee critical strike chance
		18% increased melee speed
		"The shell's weight grew into your bones"
		'''
	SetBonus:
		'''
		18% increased melee damage, but damage taken is deepened by 10%
		Striking foes condenses orbiting bubbles; at five they all collapse, detonating a heavy cavitation burst on the target
		Getting hit shatters your condensed bubbles and answers with a cavitation counter-burst (short cooldown)
		While wet, bubbles condense faster and detonate harder
		'''
}

DeepcrystalVisor: {
	DisplayName: Deepcrystal Visor
	Tooltip:
		'''
		18% increased ranged damage and 10% ranged critical strike chance
		30% chance to not consume ammo
		"Through the crystal lens, the trench shines like day"
		'''
	SetBonus:
		'''
		18% increased ranged damage, but damage taken is deepened by 10%
		Striking foes condenses orbiting bubbles; at five they all collapse into a piercing water jet toward the target
		Getting hit shatters your condensed bubbles and answers with a cavitation counter-burst (short cooldown)
		While wet, bubbles condense faster and detonate harder
		'''
}

DeepcrystalCrown: {
	DisplayName: Deepcrystal Crown
	Tooltip:
		'''
		18% increased magic damage and 10% magic critical strike chance
		Reduces mana cost by 18%
		"A murmur of the sea is sealed in the crystals"
		'''
	SetBonus:
		'''
		18% increased magic damage, but damage taken is deepened by 10%
		Striking foes condenses orbiting bubbles; at five they all collapse, launching three guided water bolts at the target
		Getting hit shatters your condensed bubbles and answers with a cavitation counter-burst (short cooldown)
		While wet, bubbles condense faster and detonate harder
		'''
}

DeepcrystalFeelers: {
	DisplayName: Deepcrystal Feelers
	Tooltip:
		'''
		18% increased summon damage
		Increases max minions by 2
		"The feelers know where prey hides before you do"
		'''
	SetBonus:
		'''
		18% increased summon damage, but damage taken is deepened by 10%
		Striking foes condenses orbiting bubbles; at five they all collapse, releasing four seeking bubbles to hunt the target
		Getting hit shatters your condensed bubbles and answers with a cavitation counter-burst (short cooldown)
		While wet, bubbles condense faster and detonate harder
		'''
}

DeepcrystalBreastplate: {
	DisplayName: Deepcrystal Breastplate
	Tooltip:
		'''
		10% increased damage and 6% critical strike chance
		"Shell traded for blade, blood traded for tide"
		'''
}

DeepcrystalGreaves: {
	DisplayName: Deepcrystal Greaves
	Tooltip:
		'''
		15% increased movement speed, further increased while wet
		Move freely through water
		"Tread the waves like solid ground"
		'''
}

SeaShrimpRelic: {
	DisplayName: Abyssal Crystal Shrimp Relic
	Tooltip: ""
}

FallenKingsCrown: {
	DisplayName: Fallen King's Crown
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Immunity to fall damage
		Hold DOWN in midair to become a crown dive and plummet
		Falling more than 25 tiles naturally also triggers the dive
		Enemies struck mid-dive are crushed by the crown
		Landing unleashes a gel shockwave; deeper falls hit harder, maxing out at 40 tiles
		The shockwave fires at most once every 1.5 seconds; the crown dims while it recharges
		The impact leaves a gel field that slows enemies inside and drains their health
		Grappling, mounting or entering liquid cancels the dive
		"The day the throne fell, weight itself became the verdict"
		'''
}

BloodfogIris: {
	DisplayName: Bloodfog Iris
	Tooltip:
		'''
		8% increased critical strike chance
		Double tap LEFT, RIGHT or UP to surge that way as blood fog, briefly invulnerable at the start
		Surges have a 1.25 second cooldown; the pupil glow dims while it recharges
		A surge ends in a 1.5 second ambush state: you sink into the fog and draw less attention
		Your next strike during an ambush is a guaranteed critical hit
		Lethal damage dissolves you into blood fog; you reform toward your cursor, briefly invulnerable and already in ambush
		The fog rebirth can occur once every 60 seconds; for 3 seconds after reforming you take 15% more damage
		"The fog has not settled, and the pupil has not closed"
		'''
}

WorldEatersMaw: {
	DisplayName: World-Eater's Maw
	Tooltip:
		'''
		All your attacks add a stack of Corrosion, up to 10 stacks; lasts 6 seconds and refreshes on every hit
		At full stacks, Corrosion strips 15 defense and sears for 20 acid damage per second
		When a corroded enemy dies, a devouring wormling bursts from its corpse to fight for you, at most one every 2 seconds
		Wormlings burrow and ambush nearby foes, biting for 2 stacks and splashing Corrosion around each breach
		Up to 3 wormlings at once, each living for 7 seconds
		"Every edge of the world is a tooth mark it left behind"
		'''
}

MirrorheartParadox: {
	DisplayName: Mirrorheart Paradox
	Tooltip:
		'''
		A mirrored heart drifts at your side
		While the mirrorheart is solid, the moment you take damage you swap places with it, dodging the hit with brief invulnerability
		Heartbeat pulses burst at both swap positions, dealing 90 base damage and confusing enemies for 2.5 seconds
		For 5 seconds after a swap, projectiles you fire are echoed by the mirrorheart at 50% damage
		Summons, held weapons and explosives are not echoed
		Paradox backlash: the next hit you take within 3 seconds of a swap deals 25% more damage
		Swaps occur at most once every 25 seconds; the mirrorheart stays translucent while recharging, with an audible cue when it turns solid again
		"In the mirror, it breaks a heartbeat before you do"
		'''
}

SwarmVortexBeacon: {
	DisplayName: Swarm Vortex Beacon
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hitting enemies stacks Bee Marks; at 8 stacks the target is caught in a swarm vortex
		The vortex grinds its victim for 5 seconds, stinging 4 times per second for 18 base damage each
		Trapped enemies are heavily slowed; bosses are only slightly slowed
		Landing more hits on the victim extends the grip, up to 8 seconds
		Only one vortex is kept at a time; when a new prey's marks fill up, the swarm moves over to it
		When the victim dies, the vortex also transfers to a nearby enemy
		Vortex stings deal 25% more damage while you carry a Hive Pack
		Stand still and the swarm returns to you, crystallizing into a wax ward over your skin
		The wax ward absorbs up to 30 damage and lingers for 5 seconds once you start moving
		A shattered ward takes 3 seconds to crystallize again
		"The Queen's beacon does not summon the swarm - it marks the next prey"
		'''
}

SoulbindingArm: {
	DisplayName: Soulbinding Arm
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Projects a curse domain around you; enemies inside take 8% increased damage from you
		Killing an enemy inside the domain harvests a soul, storing up to 8
		Souls orbit you; each one blocks an enemy projectile in your place, then expires
		Blocked projectiles turn into curseflame orbs hurled back at nearby enemies, dealing 60 base damage
		After each block, the soul ring takes 1 second to reload
		Once the ring is full it gathers briefly, then a spectral hand lunges at the strongest enemy nearby
		The hand deals 300 base damage ignoring defense, scaling with your damage bonuses
		Seized enemies take 20% increased damage from all sources for 5 seconds; regular enemies are also pinned for 1 second
		"The severed arm still harvests souls; its five fingers have never let go"
		'''
}

WhiteoutStormCore: {
	DisplayName: Whiteout Storm Core
	Tooltip:
		'''
		5% damage reduction; immune to Chilled, Frozen, Frostburn and Frostbite
		Taking damage automatically detonates a whiteout storm; lasts 6 seconds, 20 second cooldown
		The storm deals 120 base damage to nearby enemies, confusing them for 3 seconds and whiteblinding them for 6
		Whiteblinded enemies are heavily slowed and take 10 frostbite damage per second
		During the storm you gain an extra 30% damage reduction and knockback immunity, and the snow veil never blocks your sight
		Boss-class enemies cannot be confused and take a greatly reduced slow
		While running on the ground, heaves a row of ice spikes from the earth ahead every second
		Each spike deals 45 base damage and briefly chills enemies
		"Within the whiteout, the blizzard parts only for you"
		'''
}

GluttonousThroat: {
	DisplayName: Gluttonous Throat
	Tooltip:
		'''
		8% of all damage you deal flows back to you as blood beads
		Blood beads skip potion sickness, but restore at most 2% of your max life per second
		Overflow blood splatters onto the ground; Moon Bite seals the throat, and every bead falls astray
		Every 9 seconds a tongue of flesh seizes the farthest enemy within 68 tiles and drags it before you
		Bitten enemies suffer Rotsaw for 5 seconds: 40 life torn per second
		For 2.5 seconds after an enemy is dragged to you, your next strike against it deals double damage
		The executing strike also detonates any remaining Rotsaw as a burst of bonus damage
		Bosses cannot be dragged, but are still bitten, sawed and marked for execution
		"The far end of the throat has no bottom"
		'''
}

RefractionWaltz: {
	DisplayName: Refraction Waltz
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Greatly boosts aerial acceleration and turning
		Cresting a jump, double-jumping, reversing or dashing midair condenses a refraction crystal behind you
		Up to 6 crystals may exist at once; the oldest shatters to make room
		Crystals link up with prism beams in the order they were danced out, closing the loop at six
		Beam, crystal and shard damage all scale with your damage bonuses
		Each beam slices the same enemy up to 4 times per second for 35 base damage
		Enemies shattering a crystal take 70 base damage and are struck by shards dealing 40 each
		Hits inflict Refraction: the target slows and your crit chance against it rises by 8%
		"When the light-web takes shape, the one dancing to the music owns the ballroom"
		'''
}

TwinPupilTether: {
	DisplayName: Twin-Pupil Tether
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons Vision and Pyrepupil, a pair of orbiting mini mechanical eyes; their damage scales with your damage bonuses
		Vision snipes mid-range enemies with lasers: 140 base damage per shot, about one shot every 0.7 seconds
		Pyrepupil breathes cursed flames at nearby enemies: 40 base damage per gout, five gouts per second
		A cutting tether is always strung between the eyes, slicing the same enemy up to 4 times per second for 80 base damage
		Cut enemies are torn open for 3 seconds, taking 25% more damage from the pair
		The faster you move, the wider the eyes spread and the longer the tether stretches
		Double tap Down to order a cross charge: the eyes flank your cursor, dash through each other, and detonate at the crossing point
		The charge impact deals 380 and the crossing detonation 1100 base damage, with a 9 second cooldown
		"A stitched gaze, and the thread that cuts everything"
		'''
}

ProbeMatrixCore: {
	DisplayName: Probe Matrix Core
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Deploys five Destroyer probes as an escort formation that seeks enemies and fires homing lasers
		Lasers deal 55 base damage; hits on the same target build designation, and 8 stacks call an orbital strike
		The strike drops a piercing deathray from the sky, dealing 900 base damage per tick
		Targets caught in the column take at most two ticks per strike, up to 1800 base damage total
		Designation resets after each strike with a 3 second cooldown, and the impact site lingers with searing heat
		Probes shot down by enemies rebuild after about 2.5 seconds; the formation uses no minion slots
		"The iron serpent has fallen, yet its eyes still patrol the sky for you"
		'''
}

OverloadCommandCore: {
	DisplayName: Overload Command Core
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Striking enemies builds ion charge: +4 per hit, Ion Overload triggers at 100
		Stop attacking for over a second and the charge slowly drains
		Ion Overload lasts 5 seconds, increasing attack speed by 30%
		While overloaded, your hits arc chain lightning between nearby enemies, jumping up to 3 times
		Each arc deals 40% of the triggering hit's damage, decaying per jump
		Four phantom mechanical arms unfold behind you, striking in sync with your attacks
		With a melee weapon the arms sweep, each blow dealing 24% weapon damage
		With any other weapon the arms fire ion bolts, each dealing 20% weapon damage
		When the overload ends, the core overheats for 3 seconds: 8% reduced attack speed and no charge gain
		"Command authority transferred. Four arms at your service, until meltdown"
		'''
}

BloomNovaBulb: {
	DisplayName: Bloom Nova Bulb
	Tooltip:
		'''
		+30 max life and +4 life regeneration
		When struck, lashes thorn vines at your attacker or toward the incoming threat, at most once every 1.5 seconds
		Vines deal 220 to 330 base damage depending on Growth, scaling with your damage bonuses
		Snared enemies are slowed and torn for 80 damage per second; bosses are only slightly slowed
		Snared enemies that hit you suffer thorn backlash: the full damage dealt plus 120 base damage
		Thorn backlash triggers at most once per half second on each enemy
		Fighting builds Growth: more vines that snare longer
		Below 35% life, a Bloom Nova erupts: a petal shockwave of 1200 base damage sweeps and snares nearby enemies
		The bloom instantly restores 25% of your life, greatly boosts regeneration for 6 seconds, and consumes all Growth
		Spore fog follows you for 6 seconds afterward; enemies in the fog miss 25% of their attacks
		Bloom Nova occurs at most once every 60 seconds
		"Every wound waters the next bloom"
		'''
}

SolarCoreFist: {
	DisplayName: Solar Core Fist
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Stand still for half a second to enter Stone Guard stance
		While in stance, damage taken is reduced by 50% and you are immune to knockback
		Each hit taken in stance grants 1 stack of Solar Charge, plus 1 extra per 100 raw damage of the blow
		Charge caps at 24 stacks; the shell veins brighten one tier per 8 stacks
		Holding the stance for 5 seconds forces a 2 second overheat: no damage reduction, no charge, no re-entering stance
		Hold DOWN for half a second in stance to hurl a full-power fist toward your cursor with a larger solar nova
		Moving also breaks the stance and throws the fist, but at 25% reduced damage
		Throwing the fist ends the stance without overheating
		The fist deals 500 base damage, +12.5% per stack, 2000 at full charge, scaling with your damage bonuses
		The first enemy struck erupts in a solar nova, chaining six lava bursts to both sides
		At 8 or more stacks, the stance radiates a scorching aura that scales with your damage bonuses
		"The temple's sun gem still beats; the stone shell is merely its gauntlet"
		'''
}

TidalFin: {
	DisplayName: Tidal Fin
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Press [KEY] to dash toward the cursor; press again shortly after to chain, up to two dashes
		Every dash can be re-aimed, and you are fully invincible while dashing
		Each dash raises a lingering tsunami wall along its path, dealing 140 base damage per hit
		Multiple walls do not stack their hits on the same target
		The wall shoves away and slows small hostile projectiles
		The final dash raises a stationary tidal tornado at its endpoint, grinding for 200 base damage per hit
		Wall and tornado damage scales with your damage bonuses
		While it rains or you are submerged, the chain gains a third dash and all damage is boosted by 50%
		The full chain has a 12 second cooldown
		[c/2696A0:"The tide has not forgotten its duke"]
		'''
}

RiteRing: {
	DisplayName: Rite Ring
	Tooltip:
		'''
		8% increased damage, +40 maximum mana, and each lit rune grants 1% more damage
		Attacking or casting lights runes around you; at 8 runes the current rite fires automatically
		Rites rotate in order: Mirror Rite, Moonflame Laser, Star Rite
		Mirror Rite: conjures 3 pale mirror bodies, each firing 3 volleys of your held weapon's shots at 40% damage
		Summon, held-style and explosive weapons cannot be mirrored; mirrors fire rune bolts instead
		Moonflame Laser: a moon eye opens overhead and sweeps the field with a death ray
		Star Rite: a tiny planetary ring collapses, calling down 16 falling stars upon your foes
		Double tap Left or Right to spend 3 runes, tearing the veil for a short blink in that direction
		"The rite began long ago, and you are standing at the circle's heart"
		'''
}

WingsOfInterference: {
	DisplayName: Wings of Interference
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Become the wings of the Empress of Light: 3.5s of flight time by day and 4.5s by night, hold DOWN while flying to hover
		Day form: your attack projectiles trace interference light-paths as they fly
		When two light-paths cross, the intersection detonates a prism burst dealing 200 base damage
		Night form: noticeably increased movement speed and longer flight time
		At night, automatically dodge one hit, once every 48 seconds
		At night, hostile projectiles closing in on you drag auroral trails, exposing their paths early
		The instant dawn or dusk arrives, a screen-wide interference burst deals 1100 base damage and clears hostile projectiles
		"Day and night interfere at the wingtip; light collapses where paths cross"
		'''
	FormDay: It is day now: the interference weave is deployed
	FormNight: It is night now: swift auroral flight is engaged
}

BlackFlashSigil: {
	DisplayName: Black Flash Sigil
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Attacking awakens the sigil; a black flash tempo ring lights up on your chest
		The instant the ring contracts to its smallest, the judgment window opens with a sharp chime
		Hits landed within the window trigger a Black Flash: that strike deals 3x damage and always crits
		Each Black Flash adds 1 Flash Chain stack; every stack adds another 0.25x, capped at 6 stacks for 4.5x
		Higher chains quicken the tempo; the next window comes ever sooner
		Letting a window pass empty, or landing hits outside it, clears every stack
		At 4 stacks you enter Domain Sense; projectiles around you seem to slow
		Minions act on their own; they neither follow the tempo nor break the chain
		"When the flash turns black, the instant reigns over eternity"
		'''
}

FrogsparkBoots: {
	DisplayName: Frogspark Boots
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Allows flight, super fast running, and steady ice skating that won't break thin ice
		Walk on water, honey and lava, and gain immunity to the Burning debuff
		Grants 7 seconds of lava immunity, greatly reducing lava damage afterwards
		Increases jump speed by 48%, enables auto-jump, and greatly increases fall resistance
		"One frog kick, and flames clear the way"
		'''
}

CthulsparkBoots: {
	DisplayName: Cthulspark Boots
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Grants all the powers of the Frogspark Boots
		Gain cloud, blizzard and sandstorm extra jumps, increased jump height, and immunity to fall damage
		Double tap a direction to charge alongside the great eye, ramming foes out of the way
		"It floats overhead, watching every step for you"
		'''
}

NinjaCthulsparkBoots: {
	DisplayName: Ninja Cthulspark Boots
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Grants all the powers of the Cthulspark Boots
		Grants a 10% chance to dodge attacks, and the ability to climb and slide down walls
		Double tap a direction to perform a crimson shadow dash, faster and farther, trailing scarlet afterimages
		The charge bashes enemies aside like the Shield of Cthulhu, granting a moment of immunity on impact
		"The eye tied on its headband and swore never to blink again"
		'''
}

SeaShrimpSummonItem: {
	DisplayName: Crystallized Shrimp Bait
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons the Abyssal Crystal Shrimp when used at the ocean
		"Bait that sinks never comes back. Something else does."
		'''
}

SeaShrimpTreasureBag: {
	DisplayName: Treasure Bag (Abyssal Crystal Shrimp)
	Tooltip: "{$CommonItemTooltip.RightClickToOpen}"
}

SeaShrimpTestItem: {
	DisplayName: Shrimp Observation Cage
	Tooltip: Dev testing: summons the Abyssal Crystal Shrimp anywhere
}

BssBloomBud: {
	DisplayName: Thorned Bloombud
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons the Bloomsand Serpent when used on the desert surface
		"The root of the dunes grows hungry when it blooms"
		'''
}

FssFesterBud: {
	DisplayName: Festered Bloombud
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Summons the Festersand Serpent when used on the desert surface
		"The bud never died. It learned to fester"
		'''
}

BudPiercer: {
	DisplayName: Budpiercer
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Flies straight for a moment, then dips
		Striking an enemy plants a bud that soon blooms into a ring of petals
		Multiple daggers can stack buds on the same target
		Sticking into the ground blooms on the spot, spraying three needles upward
		"Under the serpent's scales, every one of them wants to bloom"
		'''
}

Thornstring: {
	DisplayName: Thornstring
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Turns any arrow into a thorn arrow
		Thorn arrows burst into short needles on both sides when they strike
		Hold right click to draw fully, then release a piercing heavy thorn arrow at 2.5x damage
		The heavy arrow blooms a ring of petals on every strike and where it lands
		"The string is a vine, the arrow a thorn, the bow a flower that refuses to wither"
		'''
}

BloomCaller: {
	DisplayName: Bloomcaller
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Sounds the horn to call a wildbloom sprout to fight beside you
		The sprout hurls sinking thorns at enemies
		After every two throws, the third attack becomes a body slam that spins into a ring of petals
		"The horn does not command. It waters"
		'''
}

Budcrown: {
	DisplayName: Budcrown
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Hold the attack key to whirl the head around you, release to hurl it at your cursor
		The head sheds needles when it strikes enemies
		Every third strike bursts into full bloom, blasting a ring of petals with heavy knockback
		"The heaviest bud blooms the loudest"
		'''
}

BloomTome: {
	DisplayName: Bloomtome
	Tooltip:
		'''
		Fires a budding bolt
		The bolt blooms into a ring of petals when it strikes an enemy or the ground
		Every fourth cast becomes a full bloom with more petals, bursting two needles upward
		"Whichever page you open, that page blooms"
		'''
}
